cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HazardNet, its forecasts or its published outputs in academic work or an operational product, please cite this repository as below."
title: "HazardNet: An Edge-native, Physics-augmented Spatio-temporal Learning for Multi-Hazard Early Warning from Multi-modal Satellite Observations"
abstract: >-
  HazardNet publishes 7- and 15-day multi-hazard outlooks for the 64 districts of
  Bangladesh across eight hazard classes, with dual-track severity values and published
  provenance for every number. Model code, dataset collection procedures, training and
  benchmarking are research-private; only results and outputs are public. Department of Agrometeorology, Bangladesh Agricultural University. Supervised by
  Dr. Ahmed Khairul Hasan; co-supervised by Dr. Md. Rakib Hassan.
type: research article
authors:
